<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="4a57e71b-9de1-54d8-b0bf-cf767cd6d926" activityNameId="e82e09b2-c753-5f81-bdf1-d8baa667b287" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Zinc coating, coils</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Zinc coating, coils
This module is applicable, if continuous zinc coating (galvanising) of hot or cold rolled strip- or wire-coils has to be inventoried. Data given per tonne of coated product are transformed by dividing them by the mean surface area of 64 m2/t (corresponding to ca. 4.2 mm thickness). The zinc coating layer is between 20 to 45 um thick. The ecoinvent module "zinc coating, pieces, adjustment per um" can be used for adjustin for thiner or thicker zinc layers of coated coils, but it 1.53 um of it have to be inventoried per um layer thickness adjustment. This is because the zinc consumption per um is higher for coil coating than it is fo piece coating. For the chemicals and the zinc, 100 km of 32t lorry transport were invnetoried. The softened industrial water is assumed to be produced at the coating plant. Continuous wire coating can be approximated with this module.;
Synonyms: hot dip coating, galvanizing, sendzimir; 
UUID: 9d201ff7-2ee4-3b8b-85df-1660a5b37ef9
Includes the process steps surface cleaning (by means of chemical and/or thermal treatment), heat treatment, immersion in a bath of molten zinc and finishing treatment. Also includes zinc input and transportation to coiling plant. Does not include the steel strip or sheet beeing coated.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Average technique for EU. 
Time period: undefined
Production volume: 12 million tonnes in 1997
Sampling: Literature 
Extrapolations: see technology
Uncertainty adjustments: Some values are from single or very few plants. For other values no data were available about the percentage of companies represented by the study citated. This was considered in the uncertainties.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_9d201ff7-2ee4-3b8b-85df-1660a5b37ef9.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
